<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicocles of Paphos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 310 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nicocles was the last king of Paphos in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, ruling in the late 4th century BCE. He founded the harbour city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nea-paphos">Nea Paphos</a> and built sanctuaries. During the wars of Alexander's successors he was suspected of dealing with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-i-monophthalmus">Antigonus</a>, and when the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I</a> surrounded his palace in 310 BCE he killed himself. His death ended the kingdom of Paphos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicocles-of-paphos.jpg" alt="Nicocles of Paphos" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nikokles_of_Paphos.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
